Description: Kidux child's screen
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This package is
 the screen a child sees once signed in, and the only program their session
 starts: their name and picture, the clock, how much time is left today, the
 learning modules an adult has enabled for them, and the buttons to lock the
 screen and to log out; and the bar along the bottom of the screen that
 takes the child between the modules they have open.
 .
 It runs as the child and decides nothing: the time is counted and the
 screen locked by kidux-daemon.
